  "studentQuestionsAI": {
    "headline": "1.3 million visits this fall; course lookups dominate, career and research content trails far behind.",
    "summary": "Between August 19 and November 17, 2026, the site drew 1,287,771 visits, nearly three-quarters of them first-time visitors. On-site searches show students are mostly hunting for specific courses, while careers, internships, and research together account for just over 2 percent of search activity?suggesting those pages exist but are not yet pulling people in.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "n": 1,
        "insight": "Careers and internships made up only 1.4 percent of on-site searches, which likely reflects thin content rather than low student interest?departments supplying graduate outcome data would give these pages something worth searching for."
      },
